  "comment": "Spec 055 \u00a73.1 and \u00a79.4. Which Node.js builds may run a TypeScript wire capture point. `audits` is the output of scripts/typescript/audit-undici-channels.mjs for one local fetch POST on each exact build (CI re-runs it on Node 22.23.5, 24.0.0, 24.4.0 and 24.22.3 and fails when a row differs). A tuple with claim `audited` only says that build publishes both body-chunk channels. A tuple is `active` once its ts-wire-passivity report (qualification/node-wire/results/passivity-<node>-<platform>.json, from the CI job of that exact build) passed every gate; report_sha256 is that file's SHA-256 (unit 055-t6). Capture is claimed only when the gates pass: TS-1U and TS-1D passed in unit 055-t17 for the active tuples (Node 24.4.0 and 24.22.3 on linux-x64-glibc, Node's bundled undici only; qualification/node-wire/results/ holds every gate's report of each); TS-1H is unit 055-t22's. A tuple left `audited` (linux arm64, musl, macOS) is not claimed and capture reports unsupported there. Node 22.x and Node 24.0.0 to 24.3.0 publish neither body channel; 24.4.0 (undici 7.11.0) is the lowest audited Node 24 build that publishes both.",
